WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
Put a human egg beside a sperm.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:06.630
The egg is about 20 times
as wide as the sperm's head.

3
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.620
Both are single cells.

4
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:12.630
And a new life starts when
exactly one of each meets.

5
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.180
So why are the egg and the
sperm built so differently?

6
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.960
In this mission, you'll watch
the moment a sperm meets the egg,

7
00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.560
and see their two membranes fuse.

8
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:26.400
Then you'll follow the two sets
of chromosomes inside the egg,

9
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.260
as they come together to start a new cell.

10
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:33.960
Your mission: explain why an egg and
a sperm are built so differently.
